WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.875
The lab runs in a test tenant, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

2
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:08.251
You need Module 2's lab done,
a Private Access test license,

3
00:00:08.251 --> 00:00:12.704
a test connector group with two connectors
on Windows Server 2019 or later,

4
00:00:12.704 --> 00:00:17.301
a test application server and a test
administrative host reachable from the

5
00:00:17.301 --> 00:00:20.030
connectors, and a
privileged test group whose

6
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.262
members have phishing-resistant
methods registered.

7
00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:26.285
Step one lists the connector
groups and connectors;

8
00:00:26.285 --> 00:00:30.924
the guide's resilience metric wants at
least two active connectors in the group.

9
00:00:30.924 --> 00:00:33.811
Step two creates the
application from the custom

10
00:00:33.811 --> 00:00:36.275
template and marks it
a Private Access app.

11
00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:40.529
Step three binds it to the connector
group and adds one segment:

12
00:00:40.529 --> 00:00:43.555
the application's host
name, its ports, and T C P.

13
00:00:43.555 --> 00:00:47.400
Step four assigns the pilot
group with the app's User role.

14
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.490
And step five puts the device and
M F A policy on it, in report-only.
